MATING MATERIAL: CONSOLIDATED NON-IV BATCH 1.0.0

Save this ZIP in ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop and extract it. Run:
  bash "$HOME/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/Mating_Material_NonIV_Batch_v1_0_0/RUN_ALL.command"

Expected runtime on the 12-core MacBook Pro: roughly 3–7 hours initially;
allow an overnight run if the drive is slow or fixed effects converge slowly.
This is an estimate, not a measured full-scale benchmark of this new batch.
The original countdown fit alone took about 57 minutes. Input verification,
bootstrap/rematch fits and report hashing add time. Each family prints progress
and its estimate; completed families are authenticated and skipped on restart.

The default target is 10 workers, an 11 GB memory budget, one BLAS thread, and
one family at a time. The countdown scheduler uses at most four fit workers;
the gap closure uses at most three. Native numerical allocations can exceed a
database's memory limit; close other memory-heavy applications for this run.
Keep the Mac on power with XT_Pro attached. caffeinate prevents idle sleep.
Keep at least 40 GiB free on XT_Pro for new caches and temporary spill.

The batch includes:
  1. All 53 responsibility specifications, including the v1.0.1 reference guard.
  2. The original random split persistence benchmark.
  3. Tenure, age-restricted Patron and condition-adjusted persistence.
  4. The arena versus pool board-state interaction.
  5. Frozen 1-in-50 first/repeat comparisons and the full-panel raw census.
  6. The separate 1-in-5 reputation, re-encounter and repayment analysis.
  7. Rating-point totals, percentile scales and own-history stakes.
  8. Patron rematch, postcertification and opportunity-level sensitivities.
  9. Rating-gap / K / RD decomposition.
 10. Finer nonparametric rating-gap profiles with exact K reference cutoffs.
 11. Countdown threshold, calendar and monthly diagnostics.

No separate responsibility run is necessary. If the exact v1.0.1 responsibility
run already finished successfully, its own authenticated checkpoint is reused.
The completed main, core persistence, core Patron and main matched-receipt
results are not rerun. Patron auxiliaries verify and use the reviewed corrected
Patron caches. This package does not update the manuscript or assert that the
whole paper is finished.

What happens if a stage fails?
The batch records the failure and continues independent families. Only the
nonparametric gap stage depends on the K/RD stage. At the end, even a failed
run produces ONE return ZIP. Return that ZIP and its .sha256 together, after
the remaining families finish. Do not send each intermediate console message.
Pressing Ctrl-C stops the run; the same command resumes verified completed
families. Some interrupted families restart their current preparation; native
countdown column/model and responsibility checkpoints preserve expensive work.
A changed completed output is reported as a failure, never silently accepted.

Outputs:
  ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/MATERIAL_NONIV_BATCH_<run>_RETURN.zip
  ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/MATERIAL_NONIV_BATCH_<run>_RETURN.zip.sha256

The report contains BATCH_STATUS.csv, all family aggregate estimates and
diagnostics, hashes, input reconciliation and REMAINING_AFTER_THIS_BATCH.csv.
Private observations, profiles and complete model logs stay on XT_Pro under:
  derived/replication/mating_material_noniv_batch_v100_PRIVATE/<run>/

The NEXT consolidated batch must rebuild the IV scores, references, histories,
exposure frames, primary and spaced estimates, both placebos, balance/entry,
subgroups, compliers, bins and receipt/Patron companions. Remaining matched
receipt companions, recipient-side Patron and the adjacent rating-payoff check
are tracked explicitly for that batch/final audit. All resulting numbers need
review before the final manuscript update.

Input safety and optimization:
This package accepts only the reviewed material build aa7e95f275c18f43...
Both main and all-source inputs are SHA256 checked. The absent old
AUTHOR_EXCLUDED_MAIN_READY_PRIVATE.json is NOT required. No source files are
overwritten. Cached game chronology, engine features, profile acquisition and
rating histories remain factual. Every eligible decision label is replaced
from the new panels before refitting. No new profiles, game API requests,
Stockfish searches or Glicko replay are launched. Dependency installation may
use the network once; production stages use local data.

Validation scope:
Synthetic integration tests check material removal, relabelling, factual
agreement, coverage, failure isolation, corrupt-checkpoint rejection and
resume. The archived responsibility and countdown numerical tests are also
run. Full production data and Mac runtime can only be validated by your run.

Options (append to the command):
  --workers 8 --memory-gb 9
  --project-root __PRIVATE_VALUE_1__
  --self-test
  --preflight-only  (authenticate inputs; do not run models)

Source provenance: repository commit 561590939aee88832480b42c5fa53428c944ca8b,
authenticated archived producers, and the corrected material-run packages.
Estimation functions retain the original specifications. Adapters change only
input binding, material eligibility/labels, reporting and orchestration.
